Modifications and new implementation
------------------------------------
Meiju MCP is a native Python implementation which ports interaction contracts
from a local Swift client. It adds a local stdio MCP interface, a browser-based
login entry point, in-memory session handling, account-scoped device checks,
restricted candidate air-conditioner profiles, and synthetic offline tests.
It is not an unmodified distribution of midea_auto_cloud.

The referenced application protocol constants are public application-level
values. They are not a user's access token, do not identify a particular user,
and do not authorize access to any account or device.

